## 🧠 Application State

The application uses one main `state` object as the single source of truth.

```javascript
const state = {
  menu: [],
  cart: [],
  search: "",
  loading: false,
  error: ""
};
```

The UI is generated from this state using the `render()` function.

```text
User interaction
      ↓
Update state
      ↓
Save state if necessary
      ↓
render()
      ↓
Updated UI
```

This prevents the application from treating the DOM as the source of data.

